WHAT THE FEATURE IS, as established by probing the DUT (not assumed):
  The DUT is an SMTP *client*. It authenticates to a remote SMTP server when sending mail
  (log email, or an operator-triggered `mail to ...`). "SMTP server authentication" means the
  DUT presents a credential to the server with the ESMTP AUTH verb. It is NOT 802.1X and has
  nothing to do with groups A/B's rig.

