================================================================================
METHOD
================================================================================
Instrument : tools/smtpsrv.py on the box, 0.0.0.0:11025, reached by the DUT at 10.38.22.33.
Trigger    : awplus# mail to cklog@ck.invalid subject <leg tag>  + one body line + Ctrl-D.
             Sending is SYNCHRONOUS on Ctrl-D ("Sending <id>... ok." / the msmtp error), so
             every leg is deterministic -- no polling, no retry window guesswork.
Grading    : the AUTH verb and the server's reply ON THE WIRE, from the server's own
             transcript, plus the DUT's own console report. Never from a `show`.
Controls   : every accepting leg is paired with a leg that must NOT be accepted, in the same
             run: an OFF baseline, a wrong-credential control per mechanism, a
             server-offers-no-AUTH control, and a removal leg.

Windows (one smtpsrv invocation each; several legs share a window):
  L0b  all mechs,   no --require-auth,  user ckmail:ckSmtp1   OFF baseline, permissive
  A    all mechs,   --require-auth,     user ckmail:ckSmtp1   the main arc, legs A1-A7
  B    all mechs,   --require-auth,     user ckmail:ckWrongPw wrong-credential controls
  C    --mech none, no --require-auth,  user ckmail:ckSmtp1   server offers no AUTH
  E    the box's own Postfix on :25 (NOT reconfigured)        real third-party server control
  F    all mechs,   --require-auth,     user ckmail:ckSmtp1   queue drain before teardown

