STEP A4 -- AUTH CRAM-MD5, correct credential (the challenge-response mechanism)
================================================================================
awplus(config)# mail smtpserver authentication crammd5 username ckmail password ckSmtp1
awplus# show mail -> Authentication : crammd5,  Username : ckmail,  Port : 11025
Trigger: mail to cklog@ck.invalid subject T33368-A4-crammd5-good

Server (srv-A.log, connection 5):
  04:09:48Z C: AUTH CRAM-MD5
  04:09:48Z ** AUTH verb from DUT: mechanism=CRAM-MD5 initial-response=no
  04:09:48Z    CRAM-MD5 challenge (cleartext): <69034.1792728588@ck-smtp>
  04:09:48Z S: 334 PDY5MDM0LjE3OTI3Mjg1ODhAY2stc210cD4=
  04:09:48Z    CRAM-MD5 decoded: user='ckmail' digest=5ba070f65aa112033aa02aed8462feca
  04:09:48Z ** AUTH CRAM-MD5 SUCCEEDED for user='ckmail'
  04:09:48Z S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
  04:09:48Z C: Subject: T33368-A4-crammd5-good   -> 250 queued
DUT console: ^DSending 20261023040947.11300... ok.
WHAT THIS PROVES, and why it is the strongest leg: the server generated a fresh, random
challenge and verified HMAC-MD5(password, challenge) itself. The DUT returned the correct
digest. The PASSWORD NEVER CROSSED THE WIRE -- only a digest over the server's challenge. So
the DUT is genuinely computing the digest from the configured password, not replaying a stored
string. (B1 below closes the loop by showing the digest changes with the password.)
STEP VERDICT: PASS.

