================================================================================
ONE THING THAT WENT WRONG, RECORDED HONESTLY
================================================================================
The first trigger attempt used tools/tb ckcon to send `mail to ... subject ...`. That command
is INTERACTIVE. ckcon sent it, the DUT answered "Type the message below and finish with a
CTRL-d", and ckcon's next command (`show mail`) was typed INTO THE MESSAGE BODY. ckcon then
waited out its full 90 s timeout and reported "cleanup: console busy or not at exec -- sent
nothing", leaving the console parked in body-entry mode. A following ckcon could not even log
in ("no privileged prompt on /dev/u2").
Recovery: tools/conkey.py was written for exactly this (no login, raw keys), the permissive
listener was started FIRST so the stranded message would be delivered rather than left queued,
and a single Ctrl-D completed it. The console returned to `awplus#`. No device state was
harmed, and the stranded message became the L0b OFF-baseline measurement above.
Cost: about 4 minutes. The lesson is in tools/conkey.py's docstring and its README entry.

